From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:40:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] usb: cdns3: cdnsp-sky1: hold the ACPI wrapper active until
 its children bind

Every O6N boot on r284 logs, for all ten USB controllers:

  cdns-usbssp CIXH2031:0N: runtime PM trying to activate child device
                           CIXH2031:0N but parent (CIXH2030:0N) is not active
  cdns-usbssp CIXH2031:0N: Enabling runtime PM for inactive device with
                           active children

v7.2.7 logs the same thing for 06-09.

Under ACPI the CIXH2031 controllers are not populated by the wrapper.
They are separate ACPI platform devices. The firmware DLKL table creates
a managed device link from CIXH2030:0N (supplier) to CIXH2031:0N
(consumer), so the child is probed from the deferred-probe work after the
wrapper's probe returns. When that probe returns, the driver core calls
pm_request_idle() on the wrapper. The wrapper has no active children yet,
so it runtime-suspends. Before late_initcall the CIX early-boot
runtime-PM gate (0003) skips the callback but still records
RPM_SUSPENDED. The gate also makes __pm_runtime_resume() return 1 without
resuming. So the pm_runtime_get_sync(dev->parent) in
__driver_probe_device() does nothing and the wrapper is still suspended
when cdnsp_probe() calls pm_runtime_set_active(). The PM core refuses
that, and the child stays RPM_SUSPENDED with an active xhci-hcd below it.
Everything reads "active" later only because pm_runtime_forbid() resumes
it after the gate opens. Until then the parent/child accounting is wrong,
and that accounting keeps the wrapper from servicing port changes.

Take a runtime-PM usage reference in the ACPI probe path before enabling
runtime PM, and drop it from ->sync_state(). The driver core calls
->sync_state() once every managed consumer of the wrapper has bound,
which is late_initcall at the earliest, when sync_state is resumed. By
then each child set itself active against an active parent, and the
children keep the wrapper active through the normal accounting. This
also matches the 7.0.12 behaviour that the existing comment requires. The
error and remove paths drop the reference if sync_state never ran. The DT
path is unchanged: of_platform_populate() binds the children
synchronously inside probe.

The global gate is left alone. Making its resume short-circuit update
runtime_status would mark devices active without running their resume
callbacks, and that unbalances clock enables in other drivers.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor glue + vendor runtime-PM gate]
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c | 46 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.h |  1 +
 2 files changed, 47 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
index ea2d032ec4e2..542ead57e473 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
@@ -784,6 +784,29 @@ static int cdnsp_sky1_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	 * inactive device with active children" warning this had silenced.
 	 */
 	device_set_wakeup_capable(dev, true);
+
+	/*
+	 * Under ACPI the CIXH2031 children are separate ACPI platform devices.
+	 * They are not created here. The firmware DLKL table links each one
+	 * to its wrapper with a managed device link, so a child probes only
+	 * after this probe returns. In that window the driver core idles the
+	 * wrapper and runtime-suspends it. Before late_initcall the CIX
+	 * early-boot runtime-PM gate skips the callbacks and also makes the
+	 * driver core's pm_runtime_get_sync(parent) a no-op, so the wrapper is
+	 * still RPM_SUSPENDED when the child calls pm_runtime_set_active().
+	 * Each child then logs "runtime PM trying to activate child device
+	 * CIXH2031:0N but parent (CIXH2030:0N) is not active".
+	 *
+	 * Hold a usage reference until every consumer of the wrapper has
+	 * bound. The driver core reports that through ->sync_state(), which
+	 * drops the reference. By then the children are active and keep the
+	 * wrapper active through the normal parent/child accounting
+	 * described above.
+	 */
+	if (ACPI_COMPANION(dev)) {
+		pm_runtime_get_noresume(dev);
+		data->rpm_hold = true;
+	}
 	pm_runtime_set_active(dev);
 	pm_runtime_enable(dev);
 
@@ -824,6 +847,10 @@ static int cdnsp_sky1_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 err_pm:
 	pm_runtime_disable(dev);
 	pm_runtime_set_suspended(dev);
+	if (data->rpm_hold) {
+		data->rpm_hold = false;
+		pm_runtime_put_noidle(dev);
+	}
 	kfree(cdns_sky1_pdata);
 	return ret;
 }
@@ -834,6 +861,10 @@ static void cdnsp_sky1_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct cdnsp_sky1 *data = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
 	pm_runtime_get_sync(dev);
+	if (data->rpm_hold) {
+		data->rpm_hold = false;
+		pm_runtime_put_noidle(dev);
+	}
 	of_platform_depopulate(dev);
 	sky1_put_addr(data->xhci_base);
 	sky1_put_addr(data->device_base);
@@ -929,6 +960,20 @@ static void cdnsp_sky1_shutdown(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * All consumers (the ACPI CIXH2031 children) have bound: drop the usage
+ * reference taken in probe and let normal runtime-PM accounting take over.
+ */
+static void cdnsp_sky1_sync_state(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct cdnsp_sky1 *data = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	if (data && data->rpm_hold) {
+		data->rpm_hold = false;
+		pm_runtime_put(dev);
+	}
+}
+
 static struct platform_driver cdnsp_sky1_driver = {
 	.probe		= cdnsp_sky1_probe,
 	.remove		= cdnsp_sky1_remove,
@@ -937,6 +982,7 @@ static struct platform_driver cdnsp_sky1_driver = {
 		.of_match_table	= cdns_sky1_of_match,
 		.acpi_match_table = ACPI_PTR(cdnsp_sky1_acpi_match),
 		.pm	= &cdnsp_sky1_pm_ops,
+		.sync_state = cdnsp_sky1_sync_state,
 	},
 	.shutdown = cdnsp_sky1_shutdown,
 };
diff --git a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.h b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.h
index 82563bd1000b..4c9a40a858c7 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.h
@@ -118,6 +118,7 @@ struct cdnsp_sky1 {
 	bool ssp_disable;
 	int axi_bmax_value;
 	struct gpio_desc *oc_gpio;
+	bool rpm_hold;	/* ACPI: usage ref held until children bind */
 };
 
 #endif /* __LINUX_CDNSP_SKY1_H */
